     "pattern",
     "fortune",
     "debt"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Patterns explain integer multiplication. As the first number goes 3, 2, 1, 0, the answers of x (-1) go -3, -2, -1, 0, then (-1) x (-1) is 1.\nBrahmagupta wrote rules centuries ago: a debt multiplied by a debt is a fortune, so negative times negative is positive.\nDivision follows from multiplication: if (-3) x 2 = -6 then (-6) divided by 2 is -3."
    }
